  "outline": [
    "Built 19 Oct 2026 (Indices clip 5) from 108.23 with 108.22's words: the question read; we want 10^x, not x — don't chase x, it is usually not a nice number (a written drop-down); the plan as maths: the key fact 10^x = 2^x × 5^x, so get 2^x and 5^x side by side and glue them; group base 5 on one side (divide both sides by 5^{2x−1}); Minus power with brackets, why the brackets (the common mistake, at the step); open the brackets, add up like terms → 5^{−x}; split the power of 2 (Add power in reverse) and a negative power flips; cross multiply (times both sides by 5^x) so 2^x and 5^x sit side by side; same power, multiply the bases: 10^x, the piece moving; 2² = 4; divide by four: 10^x = 1/4, boxed. One equation line by line, no headings, no step numbers, no Watch out.",
    "19 Oct 2026, Adrian's first notes: \"we have to find the value of 10^x, not x … without solving for x\"; \"to find 10^x, we need 2^x times 5^x. Note the base is 2 and the other base is 5\"; 5^(2x−1) moves down under 5^(x−1) (token `into`); \"To simplify the expression, we can group the fives on one side … since its divide, the powers minus\".",
